Accept and present a macOS Patch Companion.

Applies to BigShoots/PGenerator-Plus (the Pi image), not to this repository.
Carried here because the change belongs to the other repo and a macOS build is
useless without it: a stock unit validates the reported platform against
(windows|linux) and rejects the pairing request outright, so a macOS Companion
cannot pair at all.

  cd /path/to/PGenerator-Plus
  git apply /path/to/pgen-server-macos-platform.patch

On a running unit the same two files live at /usr/share/PGenerator/.

Nothing in PGICCProfile.pm branches on platform for behaviour - the three
occurrences are validation and JSON echo - so widening the two regexes is the
whole of the server change. The rest is WebUI wording and the download hint.

One choice worth explaining: the WebUI withdraws the clut and matrix
correction modes for macOS, alongside the existing rule for a pre-1.4.2 Linux
Companion, but for a different reason. The Linux rule is "this build cannot
read the active profile". macOS reads it perfectly well; the problem is that
macOS composites the patch window without an ICC conversion, so applying the
profile's inverse would have nothing to cancel against. The Companion refuses
those modes itself; this stops them being offered in the first place.

Until this is applied, a macOS Companion can still be used against the unit by
starting it with --platform-compat=linux. That pairs and heartbeats correctly
and costs only some KWin-flavoured wording in the WebUI.

--- a/usr/share/PGenerator/PGICCProfile.pm	2026-08-15 10:14:12
+++ b/usr/share/PGenerator/PGICCProfile.pm	2026-08-15 10:14:12
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@
  return '{"status":"error","message":"Pairing request is empty"}' unless(defined($body) && length($body)>0 && length($body)<4096);
  my ($client,$platform,$version)=("","","");
  $client=$1 if($body=~/"client"\s*:\s*"([A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64})"/);
- $platform=$1 if($body=~/"platform"\s*:\s*"(windows|linux)"/);
+ $platform=$1 if($body=~/"platform"\s*:\s*"(windows|linux|macos)"/);
  $version=$1 if($body=~/"version"\s*:\s*"([0-9.]{1,16})"/);
  return '{"status":"error","message":"Invalid pairing request"}' if($client eq "" || $platform eq "" || $version eq "");
  $ip="" unless(defined($ip) && $ip=~/^[0-9A-Fa-f:.]{1,45}$/);
@@ -601,7 +601,7 @@
  # so the UI needs this to say what is unavailable rather than showing the
  # missing values as a fault.
  my $platform=&webui_icc_companion_query_value($query,"platform")||"";
- $platform="" unless($platform=~/\A(?:windows|linux)\z/);
+ $platform="" unless($platform=~/\A(?:windows|linux|macos)\z/);
  my $swapchain_cs=&webui_icc_companion_query_value($query,"swapchain_cs")||"unknown";
  my $presentation=&webui_icc_companion_query_value($query,"presentation")||"unknown";
  # The Companion's own reason a requested transform is not running.
